const blogs = [
 {id:'4',title:'Why Tarbiyah Matters More Than Education in the Modern World',date:'2 March 2026',tag:'Tarbiyah in Islam',image:blogTarbiyah,imageAlt:'An open book and a young green plant in a quiet, sunlit room',excerpt:'Tarbiyah is not merely education—it is holistic nurturing that develops the mind, disciplines the heart and refines character.',body:['Tarbiyah is not merely education — it is holistic nurturing. It develops the mind, disciplines the heart, and refines character. Unlike conventional learning, Tarbiyah focuses on transformation rather than information.','At Meem Tarbiya, we believe true learning should strengthen identity, cultivate purpose, refine character and prepare individuals to face real-life challenges with wisdom.','Modern society does not suffer from a lack of information — it suffers from a lack of meaning. Tarbiyah reconnects learners with Divine guidance, helping them live with confidence, clarity and balance.','Education informs. Tarbiyah transforms.']},
 {id:'5',title:'Why Learning Arabic Is Essential for Understanding the Qur’an',date:'2 March 2026',tag:'Arabic & Quran',image:blogArabic,imageAlt:'An open Quran on a wooden stand surrounded by flowing teal and gold forms',excerpt:'Arabic opens a direct path to the language, depth and beauty of the Qur’an.',body:['The Qur’an was revealed in Arabic — not by coincidence, but by Divine wisdom. Arabic is not just a language; it is the key to revelation.','Translations provide meaning, but they cannot fully capture linguistic depth, emotional nuance, rhetorical precision and spiritual power.','When learners study Arabic, they gain direct access to Allah’s words — without filters, dilution or dependence.','At Meem Tarbiya, Arabic is taught as a living language connected to Qur’anic understanding, Seerah comprehension, intellectual clarity and spiritual reflection.','Arabic strengthens identity, sharpens thinking and deepens one’s relationship with Divine guidance. To understand the Qur’an deeply, Arabic is not optional — it is essential.']},
 {id:'6',title:'The Seerah of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ: A Timeless Guide for Modern Life',date:'2 March 2026',tag:'Seerah Studies',image:blogSeerah,imageAlt:'A sunlit desert path leading through shrubs toward distant mountains',excerpt:'Seerah is more than history—it is a living guide for character, leadership and resilience.',body:['The Seerah of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ is not a historical narrative — it is a living framework for life.','Every challenge faced today — leadership crises, emotional struggles and ethical dilemmas — already has guidance within the Seerah.','Through the Prophet’s ﷺ life, we learn emotional intelligence, patience under pressure, principled leadership, compassion with strength and balance between dunya and akhirah.','At Meem Tarbiya, Seerah is taught as a practical manual — not a storybook. Learners discover how Prophetic wisdom applies to modern family life, workplaces and society.','When the Seerah is understood properly, it does not feel distant — it feels deeply relevant.']},
 {id:'7',title:'Why Life Skills Are Essential for Faith-Based Living',date:'2 March 2026',tag:'Life Skills',image:blogLife,imageAlt:'A green notebook, prayer beads and a compass arranged for thoughtful reflection',excerpt:'Practical skills help values become consistent choices in everyday life.',body:['Faith without skill often remains unused.','Life today demands more than belief — it requires emotional regulation, ethical decision-making, communication skills, conflict management and resilience.','Islam provides guidance, but skills are needed to apply that guidance effectively.','At Meem Tarbiya, life skills are integrated with Islamic principles so learners can live responsibly, communicate wisely, respond calmly and act righteously.','Life skills transform faith into action — enabling Muslims to represent Islam with wisdom, dignity and strength.']},
 {id:'8',title:'From Knowledge to Action: The Power of Case-Based Learning in Islam',date:'2 March 2026',tag:'Learning Methodology',image:blogCases,imageAlt:'Three Islamic archways opening onto different paths through a peaceful garden',excerpt:'Case-based learning turns authentic incidents into opportunities for reflection and thoughtful application.',body:['Knowledge that remains theoretical fails to change lives. Case-based learning bridges the gap between what we know and how we live.','Through real-life scenarios, learners develop analytical thinking, ethical judgment, situational wisdom and confidence in decision-making.','At Meem Tarbiya, case studies allow students to practice applying Islamic principles to modern challenges — from family issues to social responsibilities.','This approach transforms learning into lived wisdom. Islam was never meant to stay in books — it was meant to shape lives.']}
];

